WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.989
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online Grammar, level A one.

2
00:00:06.289 --> 00:00:10.105
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:10.405 --> 00:00:15.634
Unit thirteen: Adverbs of Frequency. Today you will say how often you do things.

4
00:00:15.934 --> 00:00:18.471
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:19.433 --> 00:00:22.434
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:23.283 --> 00:00:24.238
Always.

7
00:00:25.250 --> 00:00:27.586
Always means one hundred percent of the time.

8
00:00:28.183 --> 00:00:29.893
I always brush my teeth.

9
00:00:30.483 --> 00:00:32.962
Your turn. Say: Always.

10
00:00:35.800 --> 00:00:36.708
Always.

11
00:00:37.450 --> 00:00:38.393
Usually.

12
00:00:39.383 --> 00:00:41.499
Usually means most of the time.

13
00:00:42.083 --> 00:00:43.816
We usually eat at six.

14
00:00:44.417 --> 00:00:46.732
Your turn. Say: Usually.

15
00:00:49.567 --> 00:00:50.394
Usually.

16
00:00:51.150 --> 00:00:52.314
Sometimes.

17
00:00:53.317 --> 00:00:56.291
Sometimes means not often, but some of the time.

18
00:00:56.883 --> 00:00:58.894
He sometimes walks to school.

19
00:00:59.483 --> 00:01:02.275
Your turn. Say: Sometimes.

20
00:01:05.133 --> 00:01:06.332
Sometimes.

21
00:01:07.083 --> 00:01:07.968
Rarely.

22
00:01:08.983 --> 00:01:10.693
Rarely means not often.

23
00:01:11.283 --> 00:01:13.097
She rarely watches TV.

24
00:01:13.683 --> 00:01:15.918
Your turn. Say: Rarely.

25
00:01:18.767 --> 00:01:19.756
Rarely.

26
00:01:20.517 --> 00:01:21.262
Never.

27
00:01:22.250 --> 00:01:24.609
Never means zero percent of the time.

28
00:01:25.217 --> 00:01:26.624
I never eat meat.

29
00:01:27.217 --> 00:01:29.277
Your turn. Say: Never.

30
00:01:32.133 --> 00:01:32.867
Never.

31
00:01:33.617 --> 00:01:34.455
Often.

32
00:01:35.450 --> 00:01:37.275
Often means many times.

33
00:01:37.883 --> 00:01:39.418
We often play football.

34
00:01:40.017 --> 00:01:42.576
Your turn. Say: Often.

35
00:01:45.433 --> 00:01:46.225
Often.

36
00:01:46.983 --> 00:01:48.124
How often.

37
00:01:49.117 --> 00:01:51.685
How often means a question about frequency.

38
00:01:52.283 --> 00:01:53.842
How often do you read?

39
00:01:54.450 --> 00:01:57.462
Your turn. Say: How often.

40
00:02:00.300 --> 00:02:01.580
How often.

41
00:02:02.317 --> 00:02:03.155
Routine.

42
00:02:04.150 --> 00:02:06.486
Routine means the things you do regularly.

43
00:02:07.083 --> 00:02:09.036
My routine starts at six.

44
00:02:09.650 --> 00:02:12.395
Your turn. Say: Routine.

45
00:02:15.233 --> 00:02:16.211
Routine.

46
00:02:17.000 --> 00:02:20.349
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:21.183 --> 00:02:25.786
Visal, how often do you eat rice? Always, usually or sometimes?

48
00:02:26.883 --> 00:02:36.745
I always eat rice! Adverbs of frequency tell us how often something happens: always, usually, often, sometimes, rarely and never.

49
00:02:37.850 --> 00:02:39.037
Where do they go?

50
00:02:40.150 --> 00:02:50.340
Before the main verb: I always brush my teeth. After the verb be: She is never late. They come between the subject and the verb.

51
00:02:51.450 --> 00:02:53.090
How do we ask the question?

52
00:02:54.183 --> 00:03:03.642
We ask: How often do you read? We answer: I read every day, or I sometimes read at night. They show a routine.

53
00:03:04.800 --> 00:03:06.405
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:07.250 --> 00:03:12.361
Grammar focus: Adverbs of frequency: before the main verb, after be.

55
00:03:12.661 --> 00:03:13.859
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:14.550 --> 00:03:16.364
I always brush my teeth.

57
00:03:17.250 --> 00:03:19.052
She sometimes walks to school.

58
00:03:19.950 --> 00:03:21.288
He is never late.

59
00:03:22.233 --> 00:03:27.484
Always, usually, often, sometimes, rarely and never go before the main verb and after be.

60
00:03:28.250 --> 00:03:31.158
Be careful! Don't say: He always is late.

61
00:03:33.100 --> 00:03:35.216
Say: He is always late.

62
00:03:35.516 --> 00:03:37.364
Put the adverb after the verb be.

63
00:03:38.167 --> 00:03:40.842
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

64
00:03:41.633 --> 00:03:42.542
How Often?.

65
00:03:42.842 --> 00:03:44.725
I always get up at six o'clock.

66
00:03:45.733 --> 00:03:47.814
I usually eat rice for breakfast.

67
00:03:48.800 --> 00:03:52.320
My brother sometimes walks to school, but I often ride a bike.

68
00:03:53.333 --> 00:03:56.656
My mother rarely watches TV, and my father never eats late.

69
00:03:57.667 --> 00:04:01.190
How often do you read? My routine is to read every night.

70
00:04:02.300 --> 00:04:06.302
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

71
00:04:07.150 --> 00:04:10.870
I blank eat breakfast. (100%)

72
00:04:11.170 --> 00:04:14.963
A, never. B, always. C, rarely.

73
00:04:18.500 --> 00:04:20.709
The answer is B: always.

74
00:04:21.850 --> 00:04:24.816
She blank goes to the cinema. (0%)

75
00:04:25.116 --> 00:04:29.257
A, always. B, often. C, never.

76
00:04:32.800 --> 00:04:35.113
The answer is C: never.

77
00:04:36.250 --> 00:04:37.832
Which sentence is correct?

78
00:04:38.132 --> 00:04:43.294
A, He always is late.. B, He is always late.. C, Always he is late..

79
00:04:46.833 --> 00:04:49.646
The answer is B: He is always late..

80
00:04:50.783 --> 00:04:52.597
'How often' asks about blank.

81
00:04:52.897 --> 00:04:56.353
A, place. B, frequency. C, reason.

82
00:04:59.900 --> 00:05:02.190
The answer is B: frequency.

83
00:05:03.350 --> 00:05:05.953
According to the reading, who rarely watches TV?

84
00:05:06.253 --> 00:05:09.698
A, my mother. B, my father. C, my brother.

85
00:05:13.233 --> 00:05:15.372
The answer is A: my mother.

86
00:05:16.567 --> 00:05:19.544
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

87
00:05:20.383 --> 00:05:24.206
Write two sentences about your routine using adverbs of frequency.

88
00:05:33.017 --> 00:05:34.331
Now listen to Visal.

89
00:05:34.631 --> 00:05:48.028
I always wake up at six o'clock. I sometimes eat noodles for breakfast. These sentences use adverbs of frequency. They tell my teacher about my routine and show how often I do each thing.

90
00:05:48.328 --> 00:05:49.968
Excellent answer, Visal!

91
00:05:50.883 --> 00:05:57.576
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and adverbs of frequency: before the main verb, after be.

92
00:05:57.876 --> 00:06:01.921
Today's value is time management. Plan your day and use your time well.

93
00:06:02.221 --> 00:06:05.025
See you in Unit fourteen. Goodbye!

94
00:06:05.325 --> 00:06:08.778
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

